# Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io), seeded by
# swarm-routing/.github org-sync (`citation = true`); the repository's own once
# written. Commitizen keeps `version:` in step (`.cz.toml` version_files
# "CITATION.cff:^version:"); swarm-routing/.github tools/zenodo reads the
# concept DOI from `doi:` once the first release is archived on Zenodo.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "ns3-swarm-core"
abstract: >-
  swarm-core, the shared ns-3 contrib module every swarm-routing protocol
  links against: simulator-agnostic C++20 primitives (visited path,
  little-endian wire helpers, pheromone table, route decision, link metrics)
  and the ns-3 glue they need.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Joppi
    given-names: Daniel Henrique
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6436-8174"
version: 0.0.0
# Per directory (LICENSING.md): core/ tools/ MIT OR GPL-2.0-only, the rest
# GPL-2.0-only. CFF takes a list of SPDX ids, not an expression.
license:
  - GPL-2.0-only
  - MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/swarm-routing/ns3-swarm-core"
url: "https://github.com/swarm-routing/ns3-swarm-core"
